=== T060 contract stub 1/3: compare wire format (drift detection + block) ===
NOT YET IMPLEMENTED: backstop.sh MUST accept 'compare --fast
  <fast_verdicts.json> --full <full_verdicts.json> --out <drift.json>
  [--apply --map <gate_map.json>]' -- inputs are verdicts/v1-shaped
  documents (reusing affected-set-and-verdict-cache.md's existing
  schema); DEC-17 drift = full verdict FAIL and fast verdict != FAIL
  for the same gate_id (absent from fast counts as != FAIL). Exit 0
  + stdout first line 'NO_DRIFT' when DRIFT_COUNT is 0; exit 1
  (block, release blocker per DEC-17/C-001) + one 'DRIFT gate=<id>
  fast=<verdict|ABSENT> full=FAIL' line per drifting gate (sorted by
  gate_id) + 'DRIFT_COUNT=<n>' otherwise. --out writes a
  backstop_drift/v1 document per C-002; the --apply --map pair (the
  DEC-17/AS-010a force-full write-back) is out of this RED test's
  scope -- see fixtures/backstop/README.md 'What this RED test does
  NOT cover'.

=== T060 contract stub 2/3: freshness-queue wire format ===
NOT YET IMPLEMENTED: backstop.sh MUST accept 'freshness-queue
  --registry <registry.json> --fingerprint <fp> --out <queue.json>'.
  A guard is STALE (queued) iff its stored last_verdict_fingerprint
  != <fp> (never-executed counts as stale); a guard whose stored
  fingerprint MATCHES <fp> is FRESH and is excluded from the queue
  REGARDLESS of reopens_count (§11.4.226's freshness contract
  gates membership). Queue order: reopens_count descending
  (§11.4.189 most-reopened-first) PRIMARY, staleness descending
  (older/absent last_verdict_at first) SECONDARY tie-break only.
  Exit 0 always; stdout one 'QUEUE <rank> guard=<id> reopens=<n>'
  line per queued guard in drain order, then 'FRESH_COUNT=<n>'
  'STALE_COUNT=<m>'.

